# Tool routing (lean-ctx first)

Native Read / Grep / SemanticSearch / WebSearch / WebFetch / Write / StrReplace / Delete are **denied by hooks**. Do not call them. Do not retry after a deny.

## Mapping (use immediately)

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| Read | `CallMcpTool` → lean-ctx `ctx_read` (mode `full` before edit) |
| Grep | lean-ctx `ctx_search` |
| Glob / ls / find | lean-ctx `ctx_tree` |
| Shell (when available via MCP) | lean-ctx `ctx_shell` (`devenv shell -- …` inside) |
| SemanticSearch | roam-code `roam_explore` / `roam_search_symbol`, or lean-ctx `ctx_semantic_search` |
| WebSearch / WebFetch | searxng / Context7 |
| Write / StrReplace / Edit | **lean-ctx `ctx_edit`** (or Serena edit tools if connected) |
| New file | lean-ctx `ctx_edit` with `create: true`, or Serena `create_text_file` |

Server id is typically `project-0-solana-yield-optimizer-lean-ctx` (or `lean-ctx`). Call `GetMcpTools` for the schema once, then edit.

## Edit path (no loops)

1. `ctx_read(path, mode="full")` (or Serena symbol tools)
2. Edit via **`ctx_edit`** (`old_string` / `new_string`) or Serena (`replace_regex`, `replace_symbol_body`, …)
3. On any native-edit deny or failure: switch to `ctx_edit` on the **first** failure — never retry native Write/StrReplace/Edit

## Anti-patterns

- Retrying a denied native tool
- Using native Write/StrReplace because "lean-ctx is for reads only" — in this repo, **edits go through MCP too**
- Falling back to ApplyPatch/Edit after Read was blocked
